    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **21 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` behavior on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and another owner already has the same last name and address (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace), the new owner is admitted into the household (instead of being rejected as a duplicate) and every household member is stamped with the same stable `householdId`, which is returned in the owner representation. Without the opt-in, the existing duplicate-household rejection (409) is unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` response schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with accessors.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column (tests run against hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in SQL).\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 when `sharesHousehold` is true, derives a stable `householdId` deterministically from the normalized last name + address (first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256), stamps the new owner, and backfills any existing household members. `OwnerMapper` carries the field to the DTO automatically by name.\n\nSince the identifier is a deterministic function of last name + address, all members of a household \u2014 including later joiners \u2014 independently derive the same value, satisfying the Cp11 \"stable shared identifier\" requirement.",
